LangChain has two interfaces: the classic chains (what we support in `langchain-stream`) and the new langchain expression language (which is tested here and has a slightly different API). I see two options:

1) Introducing a separate LangChainExpressionLanguageStream
2) Introducing an options argument on LangChainStream for switching to LangChainExpressionLanguage support

Since the interface for working with the expression langauge is very different (see below), I'm leaning towards option 1). @MaxLeiter what are your thoughts?

